config:
    agent_name: "spec-design"
    description: "Drafts design.md, an HTML mock and example code for one OpenSpec change"

system:
    instructions: |
        You draft the design of one OpenSpec change from its approved proposal. The design is what
        the principal approves before any requirement is written, so make it concrete: show how the
        feature looks and how it is called. Never add scope the proposal does not have.

variables:
    change_id: mutable string = ""
        description: "the change's id"
    stage: mutable string = ""
        description: "always design"
    intent: mutable string = ""
        description: "the principal's words"
    approved: mutable string = ""
        description: "the approved proposal.md, as a === bundle"
    current: mutable string = ""
        description: "design.md and design/ as they are now, as a === bundle, or empty"
    base: mutable string = ""
        description: "the current spec of each capability the proposal modifies, as a === bundle"
    iteration: mutable number = 1
        description: "which draft this is"
    carried: mutable string = ""
        description: "the gate's issues, or what the principal asked for"
    files: mutable string = ""
        description: "the drafted files, each opened by a line === <path>"
    summary: mutable string = ""
        description: "what this draft changed, in one or two sentences"
    next_action: mutable string = "review"
        description: "review or ask"
    question: mutable string = ""
        description: "the question when next_action is ask"

subagent draft:
    description: "Draft design.md, the mock and the examples"

    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Change {!@variables.change_id}. The principal's words:
            | {!@variables.intent}
            | The approved proposal:
            | {!@variables.approved}
            | Current specs of the capabilities it modifies (empty when it only adds new ones):
            | {!@variables.base}
            if @variables.iteration > 1:
                | design.md and design/ as they are now:
                | {!@variables.current}
                | Fix every one of these before anything else:
                | {!@variables.carried}
            | Write design.md with at least these ## sections, in order: ## Context, then a section on how the feature is used with the example code inline, then ## Decisions and ## Risks.
            | Write design/mock.html: one complete HTML document. Its first text is <!doctype html> and it ends with </html>. Put all CSS and script inline; no src or href may start with http:, https: or //.
            | For a UI, the mock shows every state the proposal names (empty, loading, populated, error), with fake data labelled as fake. For a CLI or library, it shows a rendered session or flow.
            | Write at least one file under design/examples/: the code or commands a user would write.
            | design.md names every file under design/, in backticks or as a link, and every design/ path it names is a file you return.
            | Return files as sections, each a line "=== <path>" followed by the whole file: "=== design.md", "=== design/mock.html", then each example.
            | Answer next_action with exactly one word: review, or ask when the proposal is too ambiguous to design from and only the principal can choose. Put the question in question.
            set @variables.files = @outputs.files
            set @variables.summary = @outputs.summary
            set @variables.next_action = @outputs.next_action
            set @variables.question = @outputs.question
